---
// Ask → card → tap → done. The approval flow, in three frames.
---

<div class="leash-steps">
  <div class="leash-step reveal">
    <div
      class="tg-card tg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Step one, you ask: a Telegram message to quill saying the Acme case-study draft is good, publish it. Quill replies that it is ready to push to blog-site, which deploys on merge, so it will ask first."
    >
      <div class="tg-head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="back">‹</span>
        <span class="who"><b>quill</b><span>bot</span></span>
        <span class="tg-ava a5">q</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tg-body" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="msg out tail">
          <p>the Acme case-study draft's good — publish it</p>
          <span class="meta">16:02 <span class="ticks">✓✓</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="msg in tail">
          <span class="name">quill</span>
          <p>Ready to push to <code>blog-site</code>. That deploys on merge, so I'll ask first.</p>
          <span class="meta">16:02</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap"><strong>You ask.</strong> The agent does the work, then stops at the consequence.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="leash-step reveal">
    <div
      class="tg-card tg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Step two, the card: quill posts an approval card requesting to push one commit to blog-site main, which deploys on merge, with Approve and Deny buttons."
    >
      <div class="tg-head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="back">‹</span>
        <span class="who"><b>quill</b><span>bot</span></span>
        <span class="tg-ava a5">q</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tg-body" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="mgroup in wide">
          <div class="msg in tail">
            <span class="name">quill</span>
            <p class="card-title">🔐 Approval needed</p>
            <p>Push 1 commit to <code>blog-site:main</code> — deploys on merge.</p>
            <span class="meta">16:03</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tg-kb">
            <span class="kb-btn">✅ Approve</span>
            <span class="kb-btn">🚫 Deny</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap"><strong>You get the card.</strong> What, where, why — and two buttons. Nothing moves without your tap.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="leash-step reveal">
    <div
      class="tg-card tg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Step three, done: the approval card now shows Approved by you at 16:04 where the buttons were, and quill confirms the post is live, noting the grant was used once, logged, and expired."
    >
      <div class="tg-head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="back">‹</span>
        <span class="who"><b>quill</b><span>bot</span></span>
        <span class="tg-ava a5">q</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tg-body" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="msg in tail" style="max-width:92%; width:100%">
          <span class="name">quill</span>
          <p class="card-title">✅ Approved · by you, 16:04</p>
          <p>Push 1 commit to <code>blog-site:main</code></p>
          <span class="meta">16:04</span>
        </div>
        <div class="msg in tail">
          <span class="name">quill</span>
          <p><b>Live.</b> Grant used once, logged, expired.</p>
          <span class="meta">16:05</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap"><strong>You tap, it ships.</strong> Every grant is scoped, audited, and expires. Deny works just as fast.</p>
  </div>
</div>
